<title>UK: Unigate Plc appoints MP as director.</title>
<headline>Unigate Plc appoints MP as director.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>British dairy and distribution company Unigate Plc said on Tuesday it had appointed John MacGregor, Member of Parliament for South Norfolk, as one of its non-executive directors.</p>
<p>MacGregor has held a number of cabinet posts including Minister of Agriculture, Fisheries and Foods between 1987 and 1989, and Secretary of State for Transport between 1992 and 1994.</p>
<p>MacGregor is also a director of Associated British Foods Plc and Slough Estates Plc.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
